        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">A Landice treadmill is a long-term purchase: a heavy, plain,
          build-to-order machine with lifetime parts cover on the residential L7 and L8, at prices
          that start above $5,000.</strong> The L7 suits most walkers and runners of average height,
          the L8 is for the tall and the heavy, and the M2 Genesis is the only one that folds.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Read the warranty for what it is — lifetime parts, one year of labour, and labour only with
          local dealer installation — and walk on one before you buy. A
          <a href="/scheels-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Scheels store</a>
          or a Landice dealer is the place to start, and our
          <a href="/commercial-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">commercial-grade roundup</a>
          shows what else the money could buy.
          </p>
